<div class="publications">
  {%- comment -%}
    Newest entries, chosen by date rather than by hand, so a new paper reaches
    the homepage without also having to be marked selected={true}.

    --max truncates after sorting (jekyll-scholar sorts in entries, then slices
    in the bibliography tag), so this really is the most recent N and not the
    first N encountered. --group_by none keeps it a flat list, which is why the
    site-wide sort_by has to lead with year: without a year group to hold the
    ordering, a Jul 2026 paper would sort below Oct 2025.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% bibliography --group_by none --max 5 %}
</div>
